    "body": "### Problem\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e2f021cb-12c6-4611-a3b6-fd6a8b1107a7\n\n```lua\n_G.test = function()\n  vim.cmd(\"normal! `[v`]\")\nend\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"d\", function()\n  vim.o.operatorfunc = \"v:lua.test\"\n  return \"g@\"\nend, { expr = true })\n\nvim.keymap.set(\"o\", \"ge\", function() end)\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n`nvim --clean -u test.lua`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAt the very least, it allows Custom {op} to evaluate whether {motion} is empty.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1828+g7e1ae5115f\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nI don't know how to test it.\n\n### Operating system/version\n\narch\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nghostty\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild",
